Suggested approach for Optimize a slow page:
1. Implement the requirement in the named App Router convention or trusted server layer.
2. Add explicit input validation and a user-friendly empty/error/denied state.
3. Exercise the normal case and at least one boundary case.
4. Run lint/tests and a production build in the target Next.js version.

Starter to adapt:
const baselineMs = 850;
const optimizedMs = 420;
const improvementPercent = ((baselineMs - optimizedMs) / baselineMs) * 100;
console.log(improvementPercent.toFixed(1) + '%');

Required static markers: baselineMs, optimizedMs, improvementPercent. These only provide a limited automatic signal; acceptance criteria must be manually reviewed.
